description:
Challenge-response in two steps, same nonces and proof tokens as REST /v1/challenge + /v1/challenge/verify. Step 1 (no signature): issues a single-use 30-second nonce for a being. Step 2 (signature over the nonce, made LOCALLY with the being's own key — never hand a private key to this server; the server only ever sees signatures): burns the nonce and, on success, returns a 300-second root-signed proof token. A replayed, used, expired or foreign nonce is refused with the same uniform 401 as a bad signature. Authenticated callers only (rule B). Auth signature over "DAXNI-REGISTRAR-AUTH-v1
{your handle}
MCP:challenge_response
/v1/challenge
{timestamp}
aud:daxni.com" (audience-bound).
